{
  "name": "Cross-post text and an image to X, LinkedIn and Facebook with Status 200 Uploads",
  "nodes": [
    {
      "parameters": {
        "content": "## Cross-post text and an image to X, LinkedIn and Facebook\n\nPost one update with one image to three networks in a single run, then see where each post landed. The networks are connected once in Status 200 Uploads, not in n8n.\n\n### How it works\n1. **Your settings** holds the post text, an optional shorter text for X and the public URL of the image.\n2. **Import image** copies the image to Status 200 Uploads and waits until it is ready.\n3. The three **Publish** nodes send one post each. Every request carries an automatic Idempotency-Key, so a retry does not post twice, as long as no post field uses $now or a random value.\n4. **Collect the answers** and **Read each post** report each network's status and link.\n\n### Setup\n1. Install the community node `@status200uploads/n8n-nodes-status200uploads` (Settings, Community Nodes). Until n8n verifies it, it installs on self-hosted n8n only.\n2. In your Status 200 Uploads dashboard, connect X, LinkedIn and a Facebook Page, and create an API key on the API page. X needs the X add-on on your plan.\n3. Create a **Status 200 Uploads API** credential with that key. In each Publish node choose the credential and your account.\n4. Fill in **Your settings** and click **Execute workflow**.",
        "height": 700,
        "width": 460
      },
      "id": "523b0f08-12d3-4bd7-9c9a-f8ec5a6277ae",
      "name": "Overview",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [-560, -240]
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "content": "## 1. Your settings\nWrite the post text and the public URL of the image (JPG, PNG or WebP, up to 20 MB). Leave x_text empty to use the same text on X.",
        "height": 300,
        "width": 440,
        "color": 7
      },
      "id": "0f51a50e-d9fc-4bab-9bfa-ed4edeaa6712",
      "name": "Note: settings",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [-40, -140]
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "content": "## 2. Import the image\nThe image is copied once and all three posts use its File ID. The node waits until the file is ready.",
        "height": 300,
        "width": 240,
        "color": 7
      },
      "id": "17780557-3318-4ee0-8acc-36a66f348ef9",
      "name": "Note: import",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [420, -140]
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "content": "## 3. Publish\nOne node per network. The automatic Idempotency-Key makes Retry On Fail safe: a post is not sent twice, as long as no field here uses $now or a random value.",
        "height": 640,
        "width": 260,
        "color": 7
      },
      "id": "540967c4-48c8-47eb-a4ec-48ec80434219",
      "name": "Note: publish",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [680, -320]
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "content": "## 4. See how it went\nThe answers are collected, then each post is read back: its network, status and link.",
        "height": 300,
        "width": 700,
        "color": 7
      },
      "id": "3225f114-3f56-4f1a-9f12-8654989b5a4e",
      "name": "Note: result",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [960, -140]
    },
